.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt LISTEN 2
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm listen
.Nd listen for connections on a socket
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.Ft int
.Fn listen "int s" "int backlog"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn listen
system call marks the stream or sequenced-packet socket
.Fa s
as accepting connections, which
.Xr accept 2
then takes.
.Pp
The
.Fa backlog
limits the connections queued and not yet accepted.
At most
.Fa backlog
are queued, and never more than 128; a backlog of zero or less means 1.
A connection to a local socket whose queue is full is refused at once.
.Pp
A local socket must be bound first.
A TCP socket that is not bound is bound to an ephemeral port; calling
.Fn listen
again on a listening TCP socket does nothing.
A local listening socket records its owner's credentials as they are at
the call, for connecting sockets to read; see
.Xr unix 4 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EADDRINUSE
Another TCP socket is listening on the port, or no ephemeral port is free.
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa s
is not an open descriptor.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The local socket is not bound, or is connected.
.It Bq Er EISCONN
The TCP socket is connected or connecting.
.It Bq Er ENOTSOCK
.Fa s
is not a socket.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The socket is a datagram or raw socket.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr accept 2 ,
.Xr bind 2 ,
.Xr connect 2 ,
.Xr socket 2 ,
.Xr unix 4
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fn listen
system call conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn listen
system call first appeared in
.Bx 4.2 .
